msgid "Blocks mined per day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:289
msgid "A low solve rate means mostly bots got the challenge and gave up. Only daily totals are stored, nothing per visitor. Days in UTC."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:290
msgid "Blocks and mining time are always counted. Challenges shown and requests let through need a persistent object cache (Redis, Memcached), so that a flood of requests never turns into database writes. Days in UTC."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:315
msgid "Visitors of protected URLs first solve a small proof of work in their browser: double SHA-256 below a target, like Bitcoin mining. Humans wait about a second once; crawlers that rotate IPs pay that for every single request. No third-party service, no tracking, nothing stored on the server."
msgstr ""

